# Deployment model

Live site: **https://instrumaps.com** (also `www` → apex 308). Hosted on
**Vercel**, project `instrumaps`, team scope `elidovrichcoding-7145s-projects`,
git-connected to `webdev-dave/build_synth_01`, production branch `main`.

## ⚠️ Pushing to `main` does NOT deploy

Auto-deploy on `main` is intentionally **disabled** via `vercel.json`
(`git.deploymentEnabled.main = false`). Commits pile up on `main` without
changing the live site. Never tell the user a push went live — verify with
`vercel ls instrumaps --prod --scope elidovrichcoding-7145s-projects`.

## Shipping to production (deliberate)

- One-off manual deploy (keeps the lock):
  `vercel --prod --scope elidovrichcoding-7145s-projects`
  (manual CLI deploys ignore the git lock)
- Re-enable auto-deploy: set `deploymentEnabled.main` to `true` in `vercel.json`
  (or delete the file), then commit + push.

## Other facts

- Feature branches still auto-build as **preview** URLs — only `main` is locked.
- Safety net: `vercel rollback <url|id>` / `vercel promote <url|id>`, or
  Instant Rollback in the dashboard. Production keeps prior deployments.
- App is currently a static export (`output: "export"`). Adding auth/DB means
  dropping that and switching to server rendering.
- Old `synth-v01.netlify.app` 301-redirects to `instrumaps.com` via
  `netlify.toml`. That file affects **Netlify only** — Vercel ignores it. Do not
  delete the Netlify site or the redirect for old links dies.
